  "solution": "The pattern followed in the given pairs is:\n\n **(First term - Second term) ×** **[**(First term - Second term) **× 2]= Third term **\n\n1) (7, 1, 72)\n\n⇒ (**7 - 1**) × [(**7 - 1**)] × 2] = 72\n\n⇒ (6) ×** [(6) × 2]** = 72\n\n⇒ 6 × 12 = 72\n\n2) (5, 2, 18)\n\n⇒ **(5 - 2)** × [**(5 -2)**] × 2] = 18\n\n⇒ 3 × [**(3) × 2] **= 18\n\n⇒ 3 × 6 = 18\n\nNow we apply the pattern on the given options:\n\n1) (4, 2, 12)\n\n (__**4 - 2**__) × [(__**4 - 2**__) × 2] = 12 \n\n (2) × [__**(2) × 2**__] = 12 \n\n __**2 × 4**__ = 12 \n\n 8 ≠ 12 \n\n2) (2, 1, 6)\n\n (__**2 - 1**__) × [(__**2 - 1**__) × 2] = 6\n (1) × [__**(1) **____**×**____** 2**__] = 6 \n __**1 **____**×**____** 2**__ = 6 \n 2 ≠ 6 \n\n3) (7, 5, 45)\n\n (__**7 - 5**__) × [(__**7 - 5**__) × 2] = 45 \n (2) × [__**(2) **____**×**____** 2**__] = 45 \n __**2 **____**×**____** 4**__ = 45 \n 8 ≠ 45 \n\n4) (3, 1, 8)\n\n (__**3 - 1**__) × [(__**3 - 1**__) × 2] = 8 \n (2) × [__**(2) **____**×**____** 2**__] = 8 \n __**2 **____**×**____** 4**__ = 8 \n 8 = 8 \n\nHence **the correct answer is option 4)**",
